---
// 🤖 How AI is used here — the transparency page. Trym, 12 Sep 2026: "transparent without saying too
// much. The code is mostly built by AI, but visuals are created by me or licensed bought visuals from
// creators with a link to them." Same day: say I make no money on it and what it costs (about 300 USD a
// month, with a visual), that I have a normal 9-5 job, that AI is in the code like in all software today
// while the visuals are bought human work or my own, and — humbly — that I recognise AI's bad sides
// (energy, slop, media made by AI) and would rather pay independent artists within a one-person budget.
// Indexed, in the sitemap, linked from the footer's host line.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'How AI is used at trymstene.com';
const description = 'AI helps write the code here, like in most software today. It does not draw the banana or its world. What it costs to run the place, who made the art, and what I think about AI.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero__banana">
      <img src="/assets/dancing-banana-transparent.gif" alt="The Dancing Banana" style="width:110px;height:auto;image-rendering:pixelated;">
    </div>
    <p class="kicker">The honest page</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title" style="font-size:clamp(2rem,8vw,3.6rem);text-transform:none;">AI, and what it does here</h1>
    <p class="hero__tag" style="text-transform:none;font-weight:500;">It helps me write the code. It does not draw the banana, and it does not run the place.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="pv">
      <h2>First, the money</h2>
      <p>I don’t make money on this. Running Banana World costs me about 300 dollars a month: the AI
        subscription, the shop platform, the domain and Cloudflare, a few ads here and there, test products
        for the shop, and small tools. The tip jar brings in five or ten dollars a month, and it all goes back
        into the place. There is no salary in it. I have a normal nine-to-five job; this is what I do with
        the evenings.</p>

      <!-- 📊 two bars, one number each. The second is small, not empty: the tip jar is real (Trym, 12 Sep). -->
      <figure class="ai-cost" aria-label="What Banana World costs a month against what it pays me">
        <div class="ai-cost__row">
          <span class="ai-cost__label">What it costs</span>
          <span class="ai-cost__bar"><span class="ai-cost__fill" style="width:100%"></span></span>
          <span class="ai-cost__val">about $300 <small>a month</small></span>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-cost__row">
          <span class="ai-cost__label">What it pays me</span>
          <span class="ai-cost__bar"><span class="ai-cost__fill" style="width:3%"></span></span>
          <span class="ai-cost__val">$5–10 <small>a month, the tip jar</small></span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Roughly, averaged over a year. It goes up in a month with a new test product or an ad.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Where AI is</h2>
      <p>In the code. Most of the code on trymstene.com and in Banana World is written with AI (Claude),
        working with me. That is true of most software you use today, from Discord and Twitch to Roblox, the
        studios behind your games, and almost any website; here I want to say it out loud. I decide what gets built, I test it, and I ship it. Nothing goes
        live because a machine said so.</p>

      <h2>Where AI is not</h2>
      <p>In the pictures. The dancing banana is mine, since 1999. The world’s places and rooms are built
        from art I bought and licensed from the people who drew it, and I take pride in that: paying for
        human work, and making my own on top of it.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The places and the rooms of Banana World: the Modern Exteriors and Modern Interiors packs by
          <a href="https://limezu.itch.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LimeZu ↗</a>.</li>
        <li>The small icons: <a href="https://pixelarticons.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pixelarticons ↗</a>
          by Gerrit Halfmann.</li>
        <li>The type: <a href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Space+Grotesk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Space Grotesk ↗</a>
          by Florian Karsten and <a href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Archivo+Black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Archivo Black ↗</a>
          by Omnibus-Type.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>No image generators are used. A few small pixel pieces are drawn in code with AI’s help, and every
        one of them goes past me before it ships.</p>

      <h2>What I think about it</h2>
      <p>AI has real problems. It costs energy and water. It fills the internet with slop. It is trained on,
        and used to replace, the work of artists and writers who never agreed to it. I use it for code with
        that in mind, and I try to keep it out of the parts that should stay human. As far as I can, within
        what one person with no funding can do, I would rather pay independent artists and creatives than let
        a model imitate them. This place and its community stay alive on that budget, and stay a place for
        everyone.</p>

      <h2>You</h2>
      <p>AI is not used to watch you, judge you or talk to you. The characters’ lines are written by hand.
        Reports are read by a person: me.</p>

      <h2>The whole list</h2>
      <p>Where AI shows up here: writing code, and reading the site’s own numbers so I can see what works.
        That is the list, and this page changes if it does.</p>

      <p><a href="/contact/">Questions? Write to me.</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .pv { max-width: 62ch; margin: 0 auto; text-align: left; }
  .pv h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 1.8rem 0 0.6rem; }
  .pv ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .pv li { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  /* 📊 the cost figure: the site’s card grammar, one hue, the small second bar says the rest */
  .ai-cost { margin: 1.2rem 0 0; padding: 0.9rem 1rem 0.7rem; border: 3px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--ink); background: #fff; }
  .ai-cost__row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 8.5em 1fr auto; gap: 0.7rem; align-items: center; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .ai-cost__label { font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .ai-cost__bar { display: block; height: 18px; border: 2px solid var(--ink); background: transparent; overflow: hidden; }
  .ai-cost__fill { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--banana); }
  .ai-cost__val { font-family: "Archivo Black", sans-serif; font-size: 0.95rem; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .ai-cost__val small { font-family: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.75rem; opacity: 0.7; }
  .ai-cost figcaption { font-size: 0.78rem; opacity: 0.7; margin: 0.2rem 0 0; line-height: 1.4; }
  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .ai-cost__row { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; }
    .ai-cost__bar { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  }
</style>
